  "classification_rules": [
    "The universe_vocabulary object is the only current canonical Universe enumeration in this registry.",
    "The legacy classification layers below remain compatibility research/display tags and never override canonical Universe.",
    "A data object may have multiple categories and tags.",
    "A Data Series has one canonical identity and may be referenced by multiple Modules without copied storage.",
    "Display categories do not override economic meaning, provenance, trust status, unit, frequency, or time semantics.",
    "Benchmark, spot-like, exchange futures, continuous futures, and options remain distinct instrument types.",
    "Macro release date semantics remain distinct from market observation date semantics.",
    "ETF amount, volume, and turnover_rate are activity proxies unless a source field explicitly represents fund flow.",
    "Structured financials, disclosure metadata, PDF originals, and parsed evidence remain distinct objects.",
    "Classification never opens formal trusted consumption."
  ],
